---
alwaysApply: true
---

Never use task.wait() with no arguments or task.wait(0) in a loop — always use a meaningful delay or switch to event-driven logic.


Never connect to RunService.Heartbeat, RenderStepped, or Stepped without storing the connection and disconnecting it when no longer needed.


Never fire a RemoteEvent without first checking the remote exists. Always nil-check before firing.


Never create UI instances (frames, labels, buttons) inside a loop or event handler that fires repeatedly. Create once on boot, reuse by toggling Visible or updating Text/properties.


Never use wait() — always use task.wait(). Never use spawn() — always use task.spawn(). Never use delay() — always use task.delay().


Never swallow pcall errors silently. Always warn the error: if not ok then warn("[ScriptName] error:", err) end.


Never hardcode player UserId or player Name as a string anywhere in server logic. Always read it from the player object at runtime.


Never write to the same DataStore key from more than one script. One script owns one key.


Never index game.Players:GetPlayerByUserId() without checking if the result is nil before using it.


Never parent a new Instance to the game tree before fully configuring it. Set all properties first, then set Parent last.


Always disconnect events when a player leaves. Store connections in a per-player table and clean up in Players.PlayerRemoving.


Never use game:GetService() inside a loop or frequently-called function. Cache all services at the top of the script.
